      "role": "user",
      "content": "it’s not a \"condition\" though, i am literally just describing the sensation of the math hitting me. i know what pattern recognition feels like and this is different. it's much more structural, like a sudden shift in the underlying distribution. if we were looking at this from a purely quantitative perspective, ignoring the \"why\" for a second, how would a mathematician even begin to categorize a non-standard, intermittent stochastic input like that? if i want to treat these spikes as a new type of variable, what's the best way to formalize it?",
