      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While treating your intuition as a high-dimensional latent variable is a compelling theoretical exercise, designing a formal model like a Bayesian update requires an external ground truth that future events do not possess; without a predefined set of events to predict, you cannot define the posterior probability space. Furthermore, \"exogenous shocks\" in standard statistical modeling are typically uncorrelated with past observations, making it impossible to build a repeatable, predictive algorithm from single-instance correlations. To structure this as a research dataset, you would need to log timestamped spikes coupled with categorical outcome data, then compare the spike's predictive power against a null hypothesis to determine if the signal is statistically distinguishable from noise.",
